CompositeDevice.SendEvent: await the command instead of blocking_send

InputPlumber 0.81.0 (and master as of 2026-10, ea60d87) handles the D-Bus
method SendEvent, an async zbus method running on a tokio worker, with
CompositeDeviceClient::blocking_write_send_event, i.e. tokio's
mpsc::Sender::blocking_send. That panics inside a runtime:

  thread 'tokio-runtime-worker' panicked at
  src/input/composite_device/client.rs:463:14:
  Cannot block the current thread from within a runtime

zbus runs each method call in its own task, so the panic kills only that
call, which never gets a reply: every SendEvent (HinterOS: the RT left
click in keyboard-mode web apps) hangs its caller. Introduced upstream by
7e76eb5 "fix(CompositeDevice): migrate to using composite device client"
(2024-06-27); not fixed upstream yet. The async write_send_event that this
uses already exists (it sends the same CompositeCommand::WriteSendEvent).
Upstream: https://github.com/ShadowBlip/InputPlumber
(src/dbus/interface/composite_device.rs, fn send_event).

--- a/src/dbus/interface/composite_device.rs
+++ b/src/dbus/interface/composite_device.rs
@@ -281,7 +281,8 @@
         let event = NativeEvent::new(cap, val);
 
         self.composite_device
-            .blocking_write_send_event(event)
+            .write_send_event(event)
+            .await
             .map_err(|e| fdo::Error::Failed(e.to_string()))?;
 
         Ok(())
--- a/src/input/composite_device/client.rs
+++ b/src/input/composite_device/client.rs
@@ -458,6 +458,7 @@
 
     /// Write the given event to the appropriate target device, bypassing intercept
     /// logic. (blocking)
+    #[allow(dead_code)]
     pub fn blocking_write_send_event(&self, event: NativeEvent) -> Result<(), ClientError> {
         self.tx
             .blocking_send(CompositeCommand::WriteSendEvent(event))?;
